* Analog tone front-end — tone-plan.md §5, up to the CVSD encoder input
*
* Pins: AUDIO CAD VCC VEE
*   AUDIO  — leveled baseband (~NOMINAL_RMS when CAD high and running)
*   CAD    — cadence gate, high = on (low mutes toward 0 through a soft RC)
*   VCC/VEE — ±12 V
*
* Param GATE: 0 = pure, 1 = soft (4 ms RC envelope), 2 = hard square gate
* Param LEVEL: scale into the encoder (trim pot stand-in)
*
* Carrier: Wien sine ~425 Hz (½ TL072). LFO: Schmitt square ~25 Hz (½ TL072).
* Wien here is only the carrier — not the dropped four-quadrant warble path.

.subckt tone_front AUDIO CAD VCC VEE params: GATE=0 LEVEL=0.11

Xcar CAR_RAW VCC VEE wien_osc R=10k C=37.4n
Xlfo LFO_RAW VCC VEE schmitt_osc Rtim=182k Ctim=100n

Cac CAR_RAW CAR 1u
Rbleed CAR 0 100k

Blfo_sq LFO_SQ 0 V = u(V(LFO_RAW))

* Soft envelope: 4 ms RC on the square (tone-plan.md §5 table)
Rsoft LFO_SQ ENV 40k
Csoft ENV 0 100n

Bpure PURE 0 V = V(CAR)
Bsoft SOFT 0 V = V(CAR) * V(ENV)
Bhard HARD 0 V = u(V(LFO_SQ) - 0.5) * V(CAR)
Bsel PRE 0 V = u(0.5 - GATE) * V(PURE)
+             + u(GATE - 0.5) * u(1.5 - GATE) * V(SOFT)
+             + u(GATE - 1.5) * V(HARD)

* Cadence mute: ~4 ms RC on CAD (envelope), multiply, then a short audio RC
* (~0.15 ms) to kill the remaining break click without eating the 425 Hz carrier.
Rcad CAD CAD_S 40k
Ccad CAD_S 0 100n
Bmute RAW 0 V = V(PRE) * V(CAD_S) / 5
Rpost RAW MUTE 10k
Cpost MUTE 0 15n

Blev AUDIO 0 V = V(MUTE) * LEVEL
Rload AUDIO 0 100k

.ends tone_front
